headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

script:post-response {
  console.log(`[${req.getMethod()}] ${req.getUrl()} -> ${res.getStatus()} (${res.getResponseTime()}ms)`);
}

docs {
  BFF-DIR-001 / SEC-AMEND-001: Six business endpoints.
  1. Sync company master, then list companies with pagination. Company/filing lists always exclude blank or missing company tickers.
  2. Backfill selected companies: metadata first, optional documents second.
  3. Query filings with original + amendments; includeContent=true includes separate bodies.
  4. All-company backfill targets only companies with nonblank DB tickers; sync companies first. Run only when required. It may take a long time.

  Backfill POST responses are SSE: started -> progress -> completed/error.
  HTTP 200 alone is not success. Check final event and failed count.
  downloadDocuments=false skips documents. Rerun to retry failed documents; completed bodies are preserved.
  There is no job status GET, runId, separate download/retry or parser-status endpoint.
  SSE events may appear in Bruno after stream completion depending on client version; curl -N supports live output.
  Job requests call SEC and change the selected database. Do not run another full backfill just to inspect the current job.
  See README.md for query variants and commands.
}
